{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"connection string configuration connection string configuration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md","fileName":"Connection String Configuration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Connection String Configuration","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Application Deployment]] [[Entity Framework Core Data Access]] [[ADO.NET Database Access]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Application Deployment","Entity Framework Core Data Access","ADO.NET Database Access","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"connection string configuration connection string configuration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md","fileName":"Connection String Configuration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Connection String Configuration","heading":"Connection String Configuration","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Connection string configuration tells the deployed backend how to reach and authenticate to its database. App Service supplies the environment-specific value so the same application artifact can connect differently in development, staging, and production.\n\nThe value is operational configuration and may contain sensitive credentials. It should not be hard-coded into the repository or exposed to the React client.\n\nIn ADO.NET, a connection string is consumed by a provider connection object and commonly names the server, database, and authentication mode. The provider interprets these key-value settings when opening the connection, so the string must match both the selected provider and deployment environment.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Application Deployment","Entity Framework Core Data Access","ADO.NET Database Access","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"connection string configuration connection string configuration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Connection String Configuration.md","fileName":"Connection String Configuration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Connection String Configuration","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[aspnetcore3andreact.pdf]]\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Application Deployment","Entity Framework Core Data Access","ADO.NET Database Access","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}